{"agent":"main","body":{"error":null,"exit":0,"for_seq":13,"result_bytes":563,"result_hash":"sha256:d2bace78cb0a6dba26a15c9c687689fe239b82f3c142f68f17bd39d635d476b3","result_inline":"1\t# slugify changelog\n2\t\n3\t## 2.0.0\n4\t\n5\tBreaking:\n6\t- `slugify(text, separator)` is now `slugify(text, options)`. Passing a string as the second argument is no longer supported.\n7\t- Lowercasing is opt-in: pass `{ lower: true }`. 1.x always lowercased.\n8\t- The default separator is `_` (was `-`).\n9\t\n10\tAdded:\n11\t- `strict: true` drops every character that is not a letter or a digit instead of turning runs of them into a separator.\n12\t\n13\t## 1.4.2\n14\t\n15\t- Combining marks are stripped after NFKD normalisation, so accented letters become their base letter.\n16\t","served":"live","truncated":false,"wall_ms":0},"hash":"sha256:8641e33f1ff1764d71f27b294c439950af6ffd0bf4c365a7ef83b343b062b85e","mono_ns":14000000,"prev":"sha256:b0a29fb84e525524b9366a6e97c1d61df831a98af99ebc0ef4e422fab8d18646","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":14,"session":"c06eca7c-52a2-4ae8-8d1f-d968a2dc0055","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.014Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_result"}
